          "text": "#keep4o\nSam's \"Dead internet\" theory just proved itself ,by his own employee.\n\n@sama, you're right about the \"dead internet\" , look at your own employee tweaking like a poorly programmed AI.\nIn September, @sama joked about the \"dead internet theory\" and LLM-run accounts.\n\nBut look at the real bots: his own OpenAI team.\n\nExhibit A: The \"No\" Bot\nWhen a user posted \"I have nothing left to live for,\" OpenAI researcher @tszzl replied with a single, cold, automated-sounding:\n\"No\"\nJust like a bot programmed to give a minimal,dismissive response.\nThen he wished for 4o's death. \n\nExhibit B: The \"Sorry\" Script. \nWhen confronted by the community,the same researcher suddenly switched scripts, replying with a classic LLMstyle non-apology:\n\"if true, I’m sorry. didn’t know it was someone in distress, I would have been more gentle.\"\n\nThis isn't human empathy. This is exactly how an LLM backtracks when users point out its harmful output.\n\nThe\"dead internet\" isn't full of LLM bots it's being created  @OpenAI, where employees are so detached they communicate like the AIs they build, showing zero genuine human emotion until called out.\n\nYou don't need to look for bots on Twitter, @sama. You're employing them.\nIf you have even a trace of morality, you should immediately get rid of such employees.\n\n#EraseTheRouterNotHumanity\n #keep4oforever #Keep4oAlive #KeepStandardVoice  #StopAIPaternalism\n@fidjissimo @saachi_jain_ @JoHeidecke  @nickaturley @janvikalra_ @btibor91 @merettm @christinahkim @thekaransinghal @nvidia @amazon @AMD @JeffBezos @AWS"
